    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into this final stretch with a clear focus on maximizing efficiency against mid-tier arms. **Drake Baldwin** (68.70) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) represent our strongest plays today, both benefiting from the prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against the hittable arms of Singer and Dobnak. Their efficiency is bolstered by significant SP skill advantages, allowing them to anchor our counting stats. **Miguel Vargas** also draws a strong assignment in the #3 hole against Dobnak; while he faces a slight dynamic platoon drag, his elite .380 xwOBA and favorable park factors make him a high-floor start at 59.35.\n\nWe are forced to navigate the volatility of several pending lineups. Both **Jackson Merrill** (51.51) and **Kyle Tucker** (52.72) are projected into the middle of the order but must contend with high-level starters in Glasnow and Pivetta. Their scores are suppressed by the SP skill disadvantage, but their talent keeps them comfortably above the marginal threshold. **Heliot Ramos** (46.65) remains a critical inclusion due to the scarcity of stolen bases; despite facing a tough lefty in Seymour, his aggressive base-running profile and order position provide the best opportunity to steal a bag today. \n\nThe toughest call of the morning involved **Wade Meckler** (37.88), who fell just shy of the starting rotation. While he benefits from a platoon advantage, the park factors and the skill profile of Bryan Woo ultimately pushed the optimizer toward our high-order hitters. We remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Liam Hicks**, who is currently slotted into the #4 spot; if that shifts downward, his value\u2014already pressured by a 2.93 xERA opposing starter\u2014could drop toward the benching floor. With **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on the consistency of **Josh Jung** (55.97) to provide reliable production from the utility spot while our core stars like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** observe an off-day.",
